// The package workflow is the design model of one durable workflow run
// (the std package workflow of the DURABLE plan, unit W0), checked by
// `ergo test models/workflow`: a breadth-first search of every state in a
// small scope. It models what crashes and the order of events can break
// in the protocol between a run's store, two workers and the receiver of
// the run's effects.
//
// The store keeps, for the run, its events (the journal), its inbox (the
// signal a sender delivered, kept until a wait takes it), its one wake (a
// revision that is ready now, or the park's timer) and the claim's lease
// with its epoch. Its writes are atomic:
//
//   - Deliver admits the signal: the signal and a ready wake (a new
//     revision) in one write, so a parked run is woken; a second delivery
//     of the same key is deduped, and a delivery to an ended run is
//     refused;
//   - Claim leases a due wake to a worker under a new epoch (a Claim after
//     Expire is a reclaim): the worker loads the events and the inbox and
//     notes the cursor and the revision it claimed;
//   - Commit appends the events the body's fold asks for next, takes the
//     signal when it wins the wait, and arms the next wake (a new
//     revision; none when the run ended), as one write under the expected
//     cursor and the claim's fence. A stale cursor (another write since
//     the load) or a lost fence (another claim since this one) refuses it
//     and changes nothing;
//   - Settle retires the wake only when it is the revision the worker
//     claimed (an ack of a stale claim, the plan's AckStale, leaves a
//     newer arm), and gives back the lease.
//
// The run's body: call A twice (two calls of one operation, A#1 and A#2,
// each with an undo), then wait for the signal or the park's timer. The
// signal finishes the run; a failed A or the timer unwinds it: each call
// done is undone, in reverse order, and the run ends failed. Replay is a
// fold of the events: a worker decides from what it loaded, never from
// memory of an earlier claim. A call's real work goes to the receiver
// with its key; the receiver dedupes on the key and answers a repeated
// key with the outcome it stored. The key is the run's id, the
// operation's name and its count, so A#1 and A#2 have two keys.
//
// A worker may crash in every state (its process dies, a new one starts
// with nothing in memory); its lease runs out (Expire) and another worker
// reclaims the wake, while the old one may still run (a paused process).
// Time passes for the park's timer (Tick). These are the plan's signals
// Deliver, Tick, Claim, Park (a Commit at the wait), Commit, Crash,
// Reclaim (Expire then Claim) and AckStale (Settle of a stale claim).
//
// Invariants (laws of Design, each `always`), on the store's durable
// state, so each holds whatever crash comes next:
//   - ReplayIsTheFold: every event is the one the body's fold asks for at
//     its place, so a replay from any cut reproduces the run;
//   - OneWinner: the wait has at most one winner in the journal;
//   - WakeCoverage: a run that has not ended has a wake;
//   - ParkHasWakeOrReadySignal: a parked run that has no winner keeps its
//     timer or has the signal in its inbox;
//   - SignalWinnerSurvives: an admitted signal is in the inbox or is the
//     wait's recorded winner;
//   - StaleAckCannotClearNewArm: a settle never retires a revision it did
//     not claim;
//   - EffectOncePerKey: the receiver applies each call's effect at most
//     once, and a call the journal records as done had its effect applied
//     (invocations may be more: Witness InvokesAgain);
//   - UndoInReverse: the unwind undoes A#2 before A#1.
//
// Mutants, each a machine whose law Breaks must hold (a shortest run to a
// state where the invariant named is false). The first three are the red
// traces of the Rivet comparison (BACKLOG/BEAM-RUNTIME/RIVET page, 3):
//   - DeleteBeforeWinner: a wait deletes the signal from the inbox in one
//     write and records the winner in a later one, the destructive wait
//     (SignalWinnerSurvives);
//   - ArmAfterPark: the park is committed with the wake retired, and the
//     timer is armed by a second write, the split park and alarm
//     (ParkHasWakeOrReadySignal);
//   - NoTailFence: a commit is not checked against the cursor and writes
//     back the inbox it captured at its load, the held queue without a
//     tail fence: a signal admitted after the load is lost
//     (SignalWinnerSurvives);
//   - AckByKey: a settle retires the run's wake whatever its revision, the
//     ack by key without a revision (StaleAckCannotClearNewArm);
//   - EarlyRelease: a worker settles its wake before its commit
//     (WakeCoverage);
//   - KeyWithoutCount: the key is the operation's name without its count,
//     so A#2 is answered with A#1's stored outcome and its effect never
//     happens (EffectOncePerKey);
//   - BlindCommit: a commit checks neither the cursor nor the fence, so a
//     stale worker and the reclaiming one both write (OneWinner and
//     ReplayIsTheFold);
//   - UndoInOrder: the unwind undoes A#1 first (UndoInReverse).
//
// Witnesses (laws of Design, each `sometimes`), so the invariants are not
// vacuous: a call invoked twice (a crash after the call, before its
// commit); the signal winning; the timer winning and the unwind ending
// failed; a stale worker beside the reclaiming one; a duplicate delivery
// deduped; a signal admitted after the timer won, kept.
//
// The scope: one run, two workers, one signal key delivered at most twice,
// one timer. Epochs, revisions and cursors are relative, as in
// models/durable: each is read only by the test "is it still the one I
// hold", so a worker keeps that test's answer (Current, Mine, Fresh) and
// every write that moves one clears it in the other worker. It is the
// claim: "proved" means proved in this scope.

// Ev is an event of the run's journal: a call done (Ok) or failed, the
// park, the wait's winner (the signal, or the timer), an undo, the end.
type Ev = Did{Call int, Ok bool} | Parked{} | Won{Signal bool} | Undid{Call int} | End{Ok bool}

// Worker is what a worker holds in memory for its claim. Current: no claim
// was made since its own (the fence). Mine: the store's wake is the
// revision it claimed. Fresh: no write since its load (the cursor). View
// is the events it loaded or committed; SawSig and Timer are the inbox and
// the wake it saw at its claim (Timer: the park's timer, due). Out is the
// answer of the call it invoked (0 none, 1 done, 2 failed). Took, Parking
// and Acked are the mutants' (DeleteBeforeWinner, ArmAfterPark,
// EarlyRelease).
type Worker {
	Has       bool,
	Current   bool,
	Mine      bool,
	Fresh     bool,
	View      []Ev,
	SawSig    bool,
	Timer     bool,
	Out       int,
	Committed bool,
	Took      bool,
	Parking   bool,
	Acked     bool,
}

// World is the store, the two workers and the receiver. Wake is 0 none,
// 1 ready, 2 the park's timer, 3 the timer due. Seen is whether the
// signal's key was admitted; Sends counts deliveries. Res is the
// receiver's stored outcome per key, Eff its effects and Inv the handler's
// invocations per call (A#1, A#2, the undo of A#1, the undo of A#2), each
// capped at 2. Cleared records a settle that retired a revision it did not
// claim.
type World {
	Ev      []Ev,
	Inbox   bool,
	Seen    bool,
	Sends   int,
	Wake    int,
	Leased  bool,
	A       Worker,
	B       Worker,
	Res     []int,
	Eff     []int,
	Inv     []int,
	Cleared bool,
}

// Act is the signals: one store or time event, or an action of worker A
// (B false) or B.
type Act =
	| Deliver{}
	| Tick{}
	| Expire{}
	| Claim{B bool}
	| Invoke{B bool, Ok bool}
	| Commit{B bool}
	| Settle{B bool}
	| Release{B bool}
	| Crash{B bool}
	| Take{B bool}
	| Arm{B bool}

let NoWake = 0
let Ready = 1
let TimerSet = 2
let TimerDue = 3

let MaxSends = 2

// The mutants and the design, as the argument of next.
let NoMutant = 0
let DeleteBeforeWinnerMutant = 1
let ArmAfterParkMutant = 2
let AckByKeyMutant = 3
let EarlyReleaseMutant = 4
let KeyWithoutCountMutant = 5
let NoTailFenceMutant = 6
let BlindCommitMutant = 7
let UndoInOrderMutant = 8

// Pos is the fold of the events: where the body is. DidN is 0 for a call
// not done, 1 done, 2 failed; Won 0 for no winner, 1 the signal, 2 the
// timer. Valid is false once an event is not the one the body asks for.
type Pos {
	Valid  bool,
	Did0   int,
	Did1   int,
	Parked bool,
	Won    int,
	Undid0 bool,
	Undid1 bool,
	Ended  bool,
}

// Step is what the body asks for next.
type Step = CallStep{Call int} | AwaitStep{} | UndoStep{Call int} | FinishStep{Ok bool} | NoStep{}

func start() Pos {
	Pos{Valid: true, Did0: 0, Did1: 0, Parked: false, Won: 0, Undid0: false, Undid1: false, Ended: false}
}

// want is the body: call A#1, call A#2, wait; the signal ends the run;
// a failure or the timer unwinds the calls done, A#2 before A#1 (A#1
// first under UndoInOrder).
func want(m int, p Pos) Step {
	if !p.Valid || p.Ended {
		return NoStep
	}
	if p.Did0 == 0 {
		return CallStep{Call: 0}
	}
	if p.Did0 == 2 {
		return FinishStep{Ok: false}
	}
	if p.Did1 == 0 {
		return CallStep{Call: 1}
	}
	if p.Did1 == 1 && p.Won == 0 {
		return AwaitStep
	}
	if p.Won == 1 {
		return FinishStep{Ok: true}
	}
	if m == UndoInOrderMutant {
		if !p.Undid0 {
			return UndoStep{Call: 0}
		}
		if p.Did1 == 1 && !p.Undid1 {
			return UndoStep{Call: 1}
		}
		return FinishStep{Ok: false}
	}
	if p.Did1 == 1 && !p.Undid1 {
		return UndoStep{Call: 1}
	}
	if !p.Undid0 {
		return UndoStep{Call: 0}
	}
	FinishStep{Ok: false}
}

func outcome(ok bool) int {
	if ok {
		return 1
	}
	2
}

// apply is p after the event e, or p made invalid when e is not what the
// body asks for.
func apply(m int, p Pos, e Ev) Pos {
	let bad = Pos{..p, Valid: false}
	let w = want(m, p)
	match e {
	case Did as d:
		match w {
		case CallStep as c:
			if c.Call != d.Call {
				return bad
			}
			if d.Call == 0 {
				return Pos{..p, Did0: outcome(d.Ok)}
			}
			Pos{..p, Did1: outcome(d.Ok)}
		case _:
			bad
		}
	case Parked:
		match w {
		case AwaitStep:
			if p.Parked {
				return bad
			}
			Pos{..p, Parked: true}
		case _:
			bad
		}
	case Won as x:
		match w {
		case AwaitStep:
			Pos{..p, Won: if x.Signal { 1 } else { 2 }}
		case _:
			bad
		}
	case Undid as u:
		match w {
		case UndoStep as c:
			if c.Call != u.Call {
				return bad
			}
			if u.Call == 0 {
				return Pos{..p, Undid0: true}
			}
			Pos{..p, Undid1: true}
		case _:
			bad
		}
	case End as x:
		match w {
		case FinishStep as f:
			if f.Ok != x.Ok {
				return bad
			}
			Pos{..p, Ended: true}
		case _:
			bad
		}
	}
}

func foldFrom(m int, p Pos, es []Ev) Pos {
	let mut acc = p
	for e in es {
		acc = apply(m, acc, e)
	}
	acc
}

func isFinish(s Step) bool {
	match s {
	case FinishStep:
		true
	case _:
		false
	}
}

func finishOk(s Step) bool {
	match s {
	case FinishStep as f:
		f.Ok
	case _:
		false
	}
}

// fold is the replay: the position the events give from the start.
func fold(m int, es []Ev) Pos { foldFrom(m, start(), es) }

func idle() Worker {
	Worker{
		Has:       false,
		Current:   false,
		Mine:      false,
		Fresh:     false,
		View:      []Ev{},
		SawSig:    false,
		Timer:     false,
		Out:       0,
		Committed: false,
		Took:      false,
		Parking:   false,
		Acked:     false,
	}
}

func zeros() []int { []int{0, 0, 0, 0} }

// world is the start: the run created with a ready wake, no worker holds
// a claim.
func world() World {
	World{
		Ev:      []Ev{},
		Inbox:   false,
		Seen:    false,
		Sends:   0,
		Wake:    Ready,
		Leased:  false,
		A:       idle(),
		B:       idle(),
		Res:     zeros(),
		Eff:     zeros(),
		Inv:     zeros(),
		Cleared: false,
	}
}

func get(w World, b bool) Worker {
	if b {
		return w.B
	}
	w.A
}

func put(w World, b bool, k Worker) World {
	if b {
		return World{..w, B: k}
	}
	World{..w, A: k}
}

// other is the worker that is not b.
func other(w World, b bool) Worker { get(w, !b) }

// bump is xs with its element i one higher, capped at 2.
func bump(xs []int, i int) []int {
	let mut out = []int{}
	for j, x in xs {
		if j == i && x < 2 {
			out = out.Append(x + 1)
		} else {
			out = out.Append(x)
		}
	}
	out
}

func set(xs []int, i int, v int) []int {
	let mut out = []int{}
	for j, x in xs {
		if j == i {
			out = out.Append(v)
		} else {
			out = out.Append(x)
		}
	}
	out
}

// slot is the receiver's index of a call: A#1 0, A#2 1, the undo of A#1
// 2, the undo of A#2 3.
func slot(s Step) int {
	match s {
	case CallStep as c:
		c.Call
	case UndoStep as u:
		2 + u.Call
	case _:
		-1
	}
}

// keyOf is the receiver's key of a call's slot: the operation and its
// count; under KeyWithoutCount the operation alone.
func keyOf(m int, s int) int {
	if m == KeyWithoutCountMutant {
		return s - s%2
	}
	s
}

// finished reports whether the worker k has nothing left to commit: it
// committed, or the run ended, or it is parked with neither the signal
// nor a due timer.
func finished(m int, k Worker) bool {
	if k.Committed {
		return true
	}
	let p = fold(m, k.View)
	match want(m, p) {
	case NoStep:
		true
	case AwaitStep:
		p.Parked && !k.SawSig && !k.Timer
	case _:
		false
	}
}

// moved clears Fresh in both workers: a write moved the cursor.
func moved(w World) World {
	World{..w, A: Worker{..w.A, Fresh: false}, B: Worker{..w.B, Fresh: false}}
}

// rearmed clears Mine in both workers: the wake is a new revision or none.
func rearmed(w World) World {
	World{..w, A: Worker{..w.A, Mine: false}, B: Worker{..w.B, Mine: false}}
}

func hasWon(es []Ev, signal bool) bool {
	for e in es {
		match e {
		case Won as x:
			if x.Signal == signal {
				return true
			}
		case _:
		}
	}
	false
}

// next is w after the action a under the mutant m (NoMutant is the
// design), or None when a is not enabled.
func next(m int, w World, a Act) Option[World] {
	match a {
	case Deliver:
		if w.Sends >= MaxSends {
			return None
		}
		let counted = World{..w, Sends: w.Sends + 1}
		if w.Seen || fold(m, w.Ev).Ended {
			// Deduped, or refused: the run ended.
			return Some[World]{Value: counted}
		}
		Some[World]{Value: rearmed(moved(World{..counted, Seen: true, Inbox: true, Wake: Ready}))}
	case Tick:
		if w.Wake != TimerSet {
			return None
		}
		Some[World]{Value: World{..w, Wake: TimerDue}}
	case Expire:
		if !w.Leased {
			return None
		}
		Some[World]{Value: World{..w, Leased: false}}
	case Claim as c:
		let k = get(w, c.B)
		if k.Has || w.Leased || (w.Wake != Ready && w.Wake != TimerDue) {
			return None
		}
		let o = other(w, c.B)
		let w2 = put(World{..w, Leased: true}, !c.B, Worker{..o, Current: false})
		let z = idle()
		Some[World]{Value: put(w2, c.B, Worker{
			..z,
			Has:     true,
			Current: true,
			Mine:    true,
			Fresh:   true,
			View:    w.Ev,
			SawSig:  w.Inbox,
			Timer:   w.Wake == TimerDue,
		})}
	case Invoke as v:
		let k = get(w, v.B)
		if !k.Has || k.Committed || k.Out != 0 {
			return None
		}
		let s = want(m, fold(m, k.View))
		let i = slot(s)
		if i < 0 {
			return None
		}
		let undo = i >= 2
		if undo && !v.Ok {
			// An undo succeeds here; a failed undo is the unwind's
			// Pending (unit W4a).
			return None
		}
		let key = keyOf(m, i)
		let first = w.Res[key] == 0
		if !first && !v.Ok {
			return None
		}
		let out = if first { outcome(v.Ok) } else { w.Res[key] }
		let res = if first { set(w.Res, key, out) } else { w.Res }
		let eff = if first && out == 1 { bump(w.Eff, i) } else { w.Eff }
		Some[World]{Value: put(World{..w, Res: res, Eff: eff, Inv: bump(w.Inv, i)}, v.B, Worker{..k, Out: out})}
	case Commit as c:
		return commit(m, w, c.B)
	case Settle as s:
		return settle(m, w, s.B)
	case Release as r:
		// A worker whose commit is refused (Conflict or Fenced) gives its
		// claim back and keeps nothing; the wake stays.
		let k = get(w, r.B)
		if !k.Has || k.Parking || (k.Fresh && k.Current) {
			return None
		}
		let w2 = if k.Current { World{..w, Leased: false} } else { w }
		Some[World]{Value: put(w2, r.B, idle())}
	case Crash as c:
		let k = get(w, c.B)
		if !k.Has {
			return None
		}
		Some[World]{Value: put(w, c.B, idle())}
	case Take as t:
		// DeleteBeforeWinner: the wait deletes the signal from the inbox
		// before it records the winner.
		let k = get(w, t.B)
		if m != DeleteBeforeWinnerMutant || !k.Has || !k.SawSig || k.Took || k.Committed {
			return None
		}
		match want(m, fold(m, k.View)) {
		case AwaitStep:
			Some[World]{Value: put(World{..w, Inbox: false}, t.B, Worker{..k, Took: true})}
		case _:
			None
		}
	case Arm as r:
		// ArmAfterPark: the timer of a committed park is armed by a
		// second write.
		let k = get(w, r.B)
		if !k.Parking {
			return None
		}
		Some[World]{Value: put(rearmed(World{..w, Wake: TimerSet}), r.B, Worker{..k, Parking: false})}
	}
}

// decide is the events a worker's commit appends, and whether the commit
// takes the signal, or None when it has nothing to commit.
func decide(m int, k Worker) Option[[]Ev] {
	let p = fold(m, k.View)
	match want(m, p) {
	case CallStep as c:
		if k.Out == 0 {
			return None
		}
		Some[[]Ev]{Value: []Ev{Did{Call: c.Call, Ok: k.Out == 1}}}
	case UndoStep as u:
		if k.Out == 0 {
			return None
		}
		Some[[]Ev]{Value: []Ev{Undid{Call: u.Call}}}
	case AwaitStep:
		if k.SawSig {
			if m == DeleteBeforeWinnerMutant && !k.Took {
				return None
			}
			return Some[[]Ev]{Value: []Ev{Won{Signal: true}}}
		}
		if k.Timer && p.Parked {
			return Some[[]Ev]{Value: []Ev{Won{Signal: false}}}
		}
		if !p.Parked {
			return Some[[]Ev]{Value: []Ev{Parked}}
		}
		None
	case _:
		None
	}
}

// commit is the one write of a worker's events, the signal it takes, and
// the next wake, under the cursor and the fence.
func commit(m int, w World, b bool) Option[World] {
	let k = get(w, b)
	if !k.Has || k.Committed || k.Parking {
		return None
	}
	// Fenced: another claim was made since this one.
	if m != BlindCommitMutant && !k.Current {
		return None
	}
	// Conflict: another write since the load.
	if m != BlindCommitMutant && m != NoTailFenceMutant && !k.Fresh {
		return None
	}
	match decide(m, k) {
	case None:
		None
	case Some[[]Ev] as d:
		// The body finishes with these events: the end is in the same
		// write.
		let p = foldFrom(m, fold(m, k.View), d.Value)
		let ended = isFinish(want(m, p))
		let evs = if ended { d.Value.Append(End{Ok: finishOk(want(m, p))}) } else { d.Value }
		let taken = hasWon(d.Value, true)
		let parks = p.Parked && p.Won == 0
		let mut ev2 = w.Ev
		for e in evs {
			ev2 = ev2.Append(e)
		}
		let inbox = if m == NoTailFenceMutant {
			// The inbox it captured at its load, written back.
			k.SawSig && !taken
		} else {
			w.Inbox && !taken
		}
		let w2 = moved(World{..w, Ev: ev2, Inbox: inbox})
		let done = Worker{..k, Fresh: true, View: ev2, Out: 0, Committed: true}
		if ended {
			// The claimed wake stays; the settle retires it.
			return Some[World]{Value: put(w2, b, done)}
		}
		if parks && m == ArmAfterParkMutant {
			return Some[World]{Value: put(rearmed(World{..w2, Wake: NoWake}), b, Worker{..done, Mine: false, Parking: true})}
		}
		let wake = if parks { TimerSet } else { Ready }
		Some[World]{Value: put(rearmed(World{..w2, Wake: wake}), b, Worker{..done, Mine: false})}
	}
}

// settle retires the worker's claimed wake when it is still the store's
// wake, and gives back the lease.
func settle(m int, w World, b bool) Option[World] {
	let k = get(w, b)
	if !k.Has || k.Parking {
		return None
	}
	let early = m == EarlyReleaseMutant && !k.Committed && !k.Acked
	if !early && !finished(m, k) {
		return None
	}
	let retire = w.Wake != NoWake && (k.Mine || m == AckByKeyMutant)
	let base = World{
		..w,
		Leased:  if k.Current { false } else { w.Leased },
		Cleared: w.Cleared || (retire && !k.Mine),
	}
	let w2 = if retire { rearmed(World{..base, Wake: NoWake}) } else { base }
	if early {
		// EarlyRelease: the worker acks first and goes on to its commit.
		let k2 = get(w2, b)
		return Some[World]{Value: put(w2, b, Worker{..k2, Acked: true})}
	}
	Some[World]{Value: put(w2, b, idle())}
}

// The invariants, on the store's durable state.

func replayIsTheFold(w World) bool { fold(NoMutant, w.Ev).Valid }

func winners(es []Ev) int {
	let mut n = 0
	for e in es {
		match e {
		case Won:
			n = n + 1
		case _:
		}
	}
	n
}

func oneWinner(w World) bool { winners(w.Ev) <= 1 }

func wakeCoverage(w World) bool { fold(NoMutant, w.Ev).Ended || w.Wake != NoWake }

func parkHasWakeOrReadySignal(w World) bool {
	let p = fold(NoMutant, w.Ev)
	!(p.Parked && p.Won == 0) || w.Wake == TimerSet || w.Wake == TimerDue || w.Inbox
}

func signalWinnerSurvives(w World) bool { !w.Seen || w.Inbox || hasWon(w.Ev, true) }

func staleAckCannotClearNewArm(w World) bool { !w.Cleared }

// done is whether the journal records the receiver's call i as done: A#n
// done, or the undo of A#n.
func done(es []Ev, i int) bool {
	for e in es {
		match e {
		case Did as d:
			if d.Ok && d.Call == i {
				return true
			}
		case Undid as u:
			if 2+u.Call == i {
				return true
			}
		case _:
		}
	}
	false
}

func effectOncePerKey(w World) bool {
	for i, n in w.Eff {
		if n > 1 || (done(w.Ev, i) && n != 1) {
			return false
		}
	}
	true
}

// undoInReverse: an undo of A#1 comes only after A#2, when A#2 was done,
// was undone.
func undoInReverse(w World) bool {
	let mut undid1 = false
	for e in w.Ev {
		match e {
		case Undid as u:
			if u.Call == 1 {
				undid1 = true
			}
			if u.Call == 0 && done(w.Ev, 1) && !undid1 {
				return false
			}
		case _:
		}
	}
	true
}

func notTheFold(w World) bool     { !replayIsTheFold(w) }
func twoWinners(w World) bool     { !oneWinner(w) }
func uncovered(w World) bool      { !wakeCoverage(w) }
func parkedBare(w World) bool     { !parkHasWakeOrReadySignal(w) }
func signalLost(w World) bool     { !signalWinnerSurvives(w) }
func clearedNewArm(w World) bool  { !staleAckCannotClearNewArm(w) }
func effectMissed(w World) bool   { !effectOncePerKey(w) }
func undoOutOfOrder(w World) bool { !undoInReverse(w) }

// The witnesses.

func invokedAgain(w World) bool {
	for n in w.Inv {
		if n >= 2 {
			return true
		}
	}
	false
}

func ends(es []Ev, ok bool) bool {
	for e in es {
		match e {
		case End as x:
			if x.Ok == ok {
				return true
			}
		case _:
		}
	}
	false
}

func signalWins(w World) bool { hasWon(w.Ev, true) && ends(w.Ev, true) }

func timerUnwinds(w World) bool {
	let p = fold(NoMutant, w.Ev)
	p.Won == 2 && p.Undid0 && p.Undid1 && p.Ended
}

func staleBesideReclaim(w World) bool {
	(w.A.Has && !w.A.Current && w.B.Has && w.B.Current) || (w.B.Has && !w.B.Current && w.A.Has && w.A.Current)
}

// deduped: the signal won and a second delivery came; only one was
// admitted.
func deduped(w World) bool { w.Sends == MaxSends && hasWon(w.Ev, true) }

func lateSignalKept(w World) bool { w.Inbox && hasWon(w.Ev, false) }

func stepWith(m int, w World, a Act) Decision[World, string] {
	match next(m, w, a) {
	case None:
		Ignore
	case Some[World] as n:
		Enter[World]{Next: n.Value}
	}
}

func stepDesign(w World, a Act) Decision[World, string]             { stepWith(NoMutant, w, a) }
func stepDeleteBeforeWinner(w World, a Act) Decision[World, string] { stepWith(DeleteBeforeWinnerMutant, w, a) }
func stepArmAfterPark(w World, a Act) Decision[World, string]       { stepWith(ArmAfterParkMutant, w, a) }
func stepAckByKey(w World, a Act) Decision[World, string]           { stepWith(AckByKeyMutant, w, a) }
func stepEarlyRelease(w World, a Act) Decision[World, string]       { stepWith(EarlyReleaseMutant, w, a) }
func stepKeyWithoutCount(w World, a Act) Decision[World, string]    { stepWith(KeyWithoutCountMutant, w, a) }
func stepNoTailFence(w World, a Act) Decision[World, string]        { stepWith(NoTailFenceMutant, w, a) }
func stepBlindCommit(w World, a Act) Decision[World, string]        { stepWith(BlindCommitMutant, w, a) }
func stepUndoInOrder(w World, a Act) Decision[World, string]        { stepWith(UndoInOrderMutant, w, a) }

// The design keeps every invariant in the scope.
type Design machine[World, Act] {
	initial: world(),
	step:    stepDesign,

	law ReplayIsTheFold always replayIsTheFold,
	law OneWinner always oneWinner,
	law WakeCoverage always wakeCoverage,
	law ParkHasWakeOrReadySignal always parkHasWakeOrReadySignal,
	law SignalWinnerSurvives always signalWinnerSurvives,
	law StaleAckCannotClearNewArm always staleAckCannotClearNewArm,
	law EffectOncePerKey always effectOncePerKey,
	law UndoInReverse always undoInReverse,

	law InvokesAgain sometimes invokedAgain,
	law SignalWins sometimes signalWins,
	law TimerUnwinds sometimes timerUnwinds,
	law StaleBesideReclaim sometimes staleBesideReclaim,
	law DuplicateDeduped sometimes deduped,
	law LateSignalKept sometimes lateSignalKept,
}

type DeleteBeforeWinner machine[World, Act] {
	initial: world(),
	step:    stepDeleteBeforeWinner,

	law Breaks sometimes signalLost,
}

type ArmAfterPark machine[World, Act] {
	initial: world(),
	step:    stepArmAfterPark,

	law Breaks sometimes parkedBare,
}

type NoTailFence machine[World, Act] {
	initial: world(),
	step:    stepNoTailFence,

	law Breaks sometimes signalLost,
}

type AckByKey machine[World, Act] {
	initial: world(),
	step:    stepAckByKey,

	law Breaks sometimes clearedNewArm,
}

type EarlyRelease machine[World, Act] {
	initial: world(),
	step:    stepEarlyRelease,

	law Breaks sometimes uncovered,
}

type KeyWithoutCount machine[World, Act] {
	initial: world(),
	step:    stepKeyWithoutCount,

	law Breaks sometimes effectMissed,
}

type BlindCommit machine[World, Act] {
	initial: world(),
	step:    stepBlindCommit,

	law Breaks sometimes twoWinners,
	law BreaksTheFold sometimes notTheFold,
}

type UndoInOrder machine[World, Act] {
	initial: world(),
	step:    stepUndoInOrder,

	law Breaks sometimes undoOutOfOrder,
}
